    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-team-1999-p6.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Observe that \\((\\sqrt[3]{2+\\sqrt{5}}+\\sqrt[3]{2-\\sqrt{5}})^{3}=(2+\\sqrt{5})-3(\\sqrt[3]{2+\\sqrt{5}})-3(\\sqrt[3]{2-\\sqrt{5}})+(2-\\sqrt{5})=\\) \\(4-3(\\sqrt[3]{2+\\sqrt{5}}+\\sqrt[3]{2-\\sqrt{5}})\\). Hence \\(\\sqrt[3]{2+\\sqrt{5}}+\\sqrt[3]{2-\\sqrt{5}}\\) is a root of the cubic \\(x^{3}+3 x-4=\\) \\((x-1)\\left(x^{2}+x+4\\right)\\). The roots of \\(x^{2}+x+4\\) are imaginary, so \\(\\sqrt[3]{2+\\sqrt{5}}+\\sqrt[3]{2-\\sqrt{5}}=\\mathbf{1}\\).",
